  Projection → WarrantyProjectionBuilder is a faithful port of the web body:
    • asString/asNumber narrowing incl. the `a ?? b ?? c` nullish chain (a present-but-empty cell stops the
      chain then narrows to nil — verified).
    • daysUntil = Math.ceil((expiry-now)/86_400_000); statusVariant (≤0/nil error, ≤90 warning, else success).
    • distance via convertDistanceFromSI(raw, unit) REPLICATED VERBATIM (web feeds the *_mi cells straight
      through the SI converter — parity over correctness; documented in Builder).
    • fmtNumber = locale-grouped fixed-fraction w/ safeNumber→0; formatDate = medium localized; coverage
      month-year = Intl month/year, pinned UTC so date-only "YYYY-MM-01" keeps its calendar month.
    • two MetricBars (time = daysUsed/totalDays w/ variant colour; mileage = current/limit w/ ratio colour,
      remaining-distance readout) + the WidgetDetailCard rows (Expiry+status badge, Days Remaining, Mileage
      Limit?, Current Mileage?, coverage ×5 Basic/Battery-Drive/Corrosion/Emissions/Body w/ Covered/Expired).
    • coverage truthiness covVal != null && !== false && !== '' (number 0 IS covered). Verified by EXECUTED harness.
  Composition → shell chrome (checkmark.shield icon + "Warranty Status" title + freshness chip + refresh +
    Open) · compact (cols≤1): shield + big days-remaining headline + "days left" + Active/Expired badge ·
    standard (2×2): time MetricBar + mileage MetricBar + coverage DetailCard.
